# Local utility

a tiny Node CLI that prints the top N most frequent words of a text file, with node:test tests

## CHECKLIST
- [ ] The CLI must accept a text file path as input and print the top N most frequent words in descending order of frequency.
- [ ] The CLI must have a flag or argument to specify N, limiting output to the top N words.
- [ ] The CLI must use node:test framework for tests located in the test directory matching pattern *.test.js.
- [ ] Tests must verify the CLI output correctness given sample text files without filesystem writes.
- [ ] The CLI must run under Node.js using the command 'node cli.js <file> [N]' or equivalent, with required flags for specifying N.
- [ ] Tests must run deterministically with no external dependencies, ensuring all behavior is verifiable from input and output.

REQUIRED RUN COMMANDS: ["node --test ./test/*.test.js","node cli.js ./fixtures/sample.txt","node cli.js ./fixtures/sample.txt 5","node cli.js ./fixtures/sample.txt --top=10","node --test ./test/topWords.test.js"]

